{
 "kind": "version",
 "id": "0.32",
 "title": "Make it yours",
 "date": "2026-11-24",
 "summary": "Version 0.32 puts the game's own tools in your hands: everything in it can be changed - while it runs, in Talos, or in mods of your own - and the changes are shared as easily as they are made. Patch 0023 opened the whole game to change: mods that replace or merge into any of its files and a Mod Editor to make them; a full mesh editor in Talos (edit mode, 120 editable shapes, booleans, a knife, loop cuts, curve deform, materials, saves kept as overrides with variants, parts bound to a character's skeleton); an animation editor; particle effects as data with an Effects editor; and the Live Editor (F10), which edits anything in the world while the game runs. It also moved Patch Notes to the title screen, put a tooltip on every control, smoothed turning and animation, slung the rifle on the back and started the browser build in 6-7 seconds. Then curve modeling (patch 0024). Then ECurves (patch 0025): every model an ECurve object, fast enough for a whole character. Then quads along the edges (patch 0026): bakes in quads that follow their edges, and settings that fit. Then joined solids (patch 0027). Then clean topology (patch 0028). Then living worlds (patch 0029).",
 "patches": [
  "0023",
  "0024",
  "0025",
